The screenshot shows COM3 is set to 9600 baud — that's the root cause of all the data issues. The FS-5000 runs at 115200. At 9600 the UART is misreading every byte, which explains the corrupted timestamps, the garbage ring buffer values, and the zero-record live captures.

Here's every setting that needs to change:

Port Settings tab (right panel):
Setting	Current	Must Be
Bits per second	9600	115200
Data bits	8	8 ✓
Parity	None	None ✓
Stop bits	1	1 ✓
Flow control	None	None ✓

Advanced FIFO tab (left panel):
Setting	Current	Must Be
Receive Buffer	14 (max)	1 — lowest
